  "notes": "{回想|かいそう}する means to look back on and reflect on past experiences, often with a nostalgic or contemplative tone.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を: {過去|かこ}を{回想|かいそう}する (to recall the past)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{回想|かいそう}している indicates an ongoing state of reminiscing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {過去|かこ}を{回想|かいそう}する: to recall the past\n- {回想|かいそう}シーン: flashback scene (in film or novels)\n- {回想|かいそう}{録|ろく}: memoirs, reminiscences\n- {回想|かいそう}にふける: to be lost in reminiscence\n\nREGISTER:\nLiterary and somewhat formal. Common in written narratives, film criticism, and memoir contexts. In casual speech, {思|おも}い{出|だ}す (to remember) or {振|ふ}り{返|かえ}る (to look back) are more natural.",
